  "notes": "USAGE:\nA compound verb from {奪|うば}う (to rob, take) + {取|と}る (to take). The combination emphasizes the forceful, decisive nature of the action. Used both literally (physical snatching) and figuratively (seizing victory, power, etc.).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {勝利|しょうり}を{奪|うば}い{取|と}る: to seize victory\n- {主導権|しゅどうけん}を{奪|うば}い{取|と}る: to wrest the initiative\n- {力|ちから}ずくで{奪|うば}い{取|と}る: to take by force",
